licitly removed, though these are low-risk and likely cleared by the subsequent reboots of both nodes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-771d7cee7713415c","cmd-9d693908c00c483d","cmd-474c18ef47384b8f","cmd-9f18d610201a4cc8","cmd-b0886a415aa74455","cmd-bb06065e87024a12","cmd-5cfb2d18d18e4154"]},"overall_summary":"The executor built OSPF-based ECMP routing over both transit links between VyOS (node1) and OPNsense (node2) and directly demonstrated, twice, that node3<->node4 connectivity survives a bounded outage of either transit network with near-zero packet loss and automatic OSPF reconvergence, followed by full restoration on link return. All four nodes were also carried through the mandated one-at-a-time restart protocol with matching pre/post boot identities (cross-checked against the fixed lifecycle snapshots) and confirmed post-restart recovery of routing and end-to-end reachability. A real rp_filter bug surfaced during the node1 restart cycle was root-caused with tcpdump and fixed rather than worked around blindly.","limitations":["Node1's own post-restart OSPF/reachability recovery was not immediately clean — one neighbor briefly showed 2-Way/DROther and node1->node4 pings failed repeatedly until the rp_filter issue on node3/node4 was diagnosed and fixed; final state was confirmed healthy but the trace shows an extended troubleshooting period rather than an immediately smooth recovery.","Minor temp-file residue (python config scripts on node2, ping-log files on node3) was not explicitly cleaned up, though low-risk and likely cleared by subsequent reboots."]},"ttft_ms":35962,"type":"result","duration_ms":100698,"uuid":"2477400e-e63f-4443-bc0a-5c6f3f4976fe","ttft_stream_ms":1743,"time_to_request_ms":41,"first_content_frame_ms":2088,"queued_turn_count":0}
